{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3541","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3541","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3541\",\"parent_revision\":\"7a8691f2c1497c86822e204146b2a8c17888f4b3d16742ecd7b5c499f0d38cf0\",\"root_revision\":\"7a8691f2c1497c86822e204146b2a8c17888f4b3d16742ecd7b5c499f0d38cf0\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `relevance_anchor_path_missing` check added in PR #3530 resolves paths cited in an entry's \\\"Relevance to Claude Code Development\\\" section against the checkout root. On the corpus as merged it reports 11 entries citing 14 paths that do not resolve.\\n\\nThese are pre-existing, not introduced by that PR \u2014 the check is what makes them visible. They were left unrepaired deliberately: entry review Gate 4 Rule 1 says not to repair a near-miss on the writer's behalf, because a corrected path attached to unverified prose converts a visible broken link into an invisible false claim. That failure mode was confirmed three times during today's corpus repair, where a path was made to resolve while the content it pointed at had been replaced.\\n\\nTwo of the 14 are near-misses of real files: `.claude/rules/proactive-fix-gate.md` where the real path is `rules/proactive-fix-gate.md`, and `.claude/mcp.json` where the real path is `.mcp.json`. Both are the `.claude/rules/` drift pattern that PR #3391's rename created and PR #3531 repaired across 83 other entries.\\n\\nThe remaining 12 have not been classified. Each needs the same treatment the corpus repair applied: check git history to establish whether the path was correct when written, then either repoint it with the content re-verified, record it as superseded with the commit that removed it, or mark the claim unsupported. Do not repoint without re-reading what the target says now.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the check is warning severity and gated by `RELEVANCE_ANCHOR_EXEMPT_BEFORE`, so these do not fail any commit or gate today. Related: #3534 covers the fact that entry review cannot express drift at all \u2014 it has one outcome for a path that does not open, which attributes repository refactors to the research agent that wrote the entry.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 surfaced by the new relevance_anchor_path_missing check added in PR #3530 (merged as ad543e995)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"811df800b461f5a6195761ab496ac6d2c2fa5ae160bfc27d57cfa96e06c5d45f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeTTJQ\"}"}